# The repository is used from Linux, macOS and Windows, and three things on the Windows side
# read repository files as *data* rather than as source: `windows/unity-capture.sha256` (fed to
# sha256sum), `VERSION` (read by windows/package.cmake to name the installer) and the NSIS
# scripts. A CRLF checkout turns the checksum file's names into "UnityCaptureFilter32.dll\r",
# which sha256sum reports as a missing file, and would put a carriage return in the installer's
# version string. Keep text to LF everywhere; a .bat file is the one format that wants CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.jks binary
